{"id":"C2.3.4","doc":"C","title":"Restrictions for GPIOs and RTC_GPIOs","words":311,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"All IO pins of ESP32-S3 have GPIO and some have RTC_GPIO pin functions."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"However, the IO pins are multiplexed and can be configured for different purposes based on the requirements."}]},{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Some IOs have restrictions for usage."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"It is essential to consider the multiplexed nature and the limitations when using these IO pins."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In tables of this chapter, some pin functions are in red ("},{"t":"code","v":"[R]"},{"t":"text","v":") or yellow ("},{"t":"code","v":"[Y]"},{"t":"text","v":")."}]},{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"These functions indicate pins that require extra caution when used as GPIO / GPIO:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Red ("},{"t":"code","v":"[R]"},{"t":"text","v":") IO Pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":" - allocated for communication with in-package flash/"},{"t":"block","v":"PSRAM","id":"flash-psram"},{"t":"text","v":" and NOT recommended for other uses."}],"warn":true},{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For details, see "},{"t":"xref","id":"C2.6","c":[{"t":"text","v":"C2.6 Pin Mapping Between Chip and Flash/PSRAM"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"b","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Yellow ("},{"t":"code","v":"[Y]"},{"t":"text","v":") IO Pins"}]},{"t":"text","v":" - have one of the following important functions:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Strapping pins - need to be at certain logic levels at startup."}]},{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"See "},{"t":"xref","id":"C3","c":[{"t":"text","v":"C3 Boot Configurations"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Note: Strapping pins are highlighted by "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"Pin Name"}]},{"t":"text","v":" or configurations "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"At Reset"}]},{"t":"text","v":", instead of the pin functions."}],"warn":true}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":13,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"USB_D+/- - by default, connected to the "},{"t":"block","v":"USB Serial/JTAG","id":"usb-serial-jtag"},{"t":"text","v":" Controller."}]},{"n":14,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"To function as GPIOs, these pins need to be reconfigured via the "},{"t":"field","v":"IO_MUX_MCU_SEL"},{"t":"text","v":" bit (see "},{"t":"link","href":"https://espressif.com/documentation/esp32-s3_technical_reference_manual_en.pdf#iomuxgpio","c":[{"t":"text","v":"ESP32-S3 Technical Reference Manual"}]},{"t":"text","v":" > Chapter "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX and GPIO Matrix"}]},{"t":"text","v":" for details)."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":15,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"JTAG interface - often used for debugging."}]},{"n":16,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"See Table 2-4 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX Functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]},{"n":17,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"To free these pins up, the pin functions USB_D+/- of the USB Serial/JTAG Controller can be used instead."}]},{"n":18,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"See also "},{"t":"xref","id":"C3.4","c":[{"t":"text","v":"C3.4 JTAG Signal Source Control"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":19,"c":[{"t":"block","v":"UART0","id":"uart"},{"t":"text","v":" interface - often used for debugging."}]},{"n":20,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"See Table 2-4 "},{"t":"i","c":[{"t":"text","v":"IO MUX Functions"}]},{"t":"text","v":"."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":21,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"8-line "},{"t":"block","v":"SPI","id":"spi"},{"t":"text","v":" interface - no restrictions, unless the chip is connected to flash/PSRAM using 8-line SPI mode."}]}]}]]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":22,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"For more information about assigning pins, please see "},{"t":"xref","id":"C2.3.5","c":[{"t":"text","v":"C2.3.5 Peripheral Pin Assignment"}]},{"t":"text","v":" and "},{"t":"xref","id":"C8","c":[{"t"